  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Segments \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\) intersect at point \\(O\\), with \\(OA=OC\\), \\(OB=OD\\), and \\(AB=7\\). Find the length of \\(CD\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "7",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\angle AOB=\\angle COD\\) (vertically opposite angles), \\(OA=OC\\), and \\(OB=OD\\), so \\(\\triangle AOB\\cong\\triangle COD\\) by SAS. Thus, \\(CD=AB=7\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Recognize a parallelogram\n\nThe equalities \\(OA=OC\\) and \\(OB=OD\\) show that \\(O\\) is the midpoint of both \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\). These are the diagonals of quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\), so its diagonals bisect each other. A quadrilateral whose diagonals bisect each other is a parallelogram. Its opposite sides are equal, giving \\(CD=AB=7\\).",
